From 6e9abddf2efd7557cb650c5712a1eaf700e38c5c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "R.R. Sinha" <rrsinha378@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 17:54:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Stop scoring sites that were never fetched; stop leaking URLs

The engine could report a confident score for a site it never loaded.

Root cause: every check asked "which pages have this problem?" and scored a
pass when the answer was an empty list. An empty list also means "no pages
were checked", so a crawl that fetched nothing returned On-page 100,
Content 100 and 81/100 overall, with the detail line "Every page has a
title of a sensible length."

What changed:

- Analyzer.run() raises AuditError when no page was fetched, and again when
  every page is rendered in the browser. main() exits 2 and writes no PDF.
- New "skip" status for checks with nothing to inspect. Skipped checks are
  removed from both numerator and denominator, categories with no measured
  check are dropped and the remaining weights renormalised. Coverage is
  computed and the run refuses to publish a score below 50%.
- --label no longer rewrites the host of every finding. A staging crawl was
  reporting "8 of 8 pages served over plain HTTP" about the live domain.
  The label is a caption; measured URLs print as fetched, with a note
  saying which address was measured.
- HTTPS is "not measured" on a local or private origin instead of failed.
- JS-rendered pages are detected and excluded from on-page checks, with a
  new check that reports them. Previously an SPA scored as an empty page.
- Failed pages stay in the page-by-page table with their status and no
  score; they used to vanish, so the report claimed more pages than it
  showed and every hidden page looked clean.
- Redaction: URL credentials, and query values for tokens, keys, signatures,
  sessions, OTPs and passwords, are stripped at one choke point before
  anything is printed, exported or rendered. Response headers drop
  Set-Cookie / Cookie / Authorization. JSON exports carry no page bodies,
  headers, cookies or raw JSON-LD.
- Politeness delay now applies after failed requests too; 404 probe URL is
  stable across runs; nested-quote f-string that required Python 3.12 is
  gone, so the stated 3.9+ floor is true again.
- 17 regression tests covering the guarantees above.
